Compilers other than GCC and Clang get empty symbol aliases. Upstream defines them only for GNU
compilers; MSVC then sees an undeclared macro. The aliases only name the long-double and ldexp forms,
which the UCRT subset does not export; the names header maps ldexp to scalbn.

